- Online stepwise failure detection on multi-step LLM trajectories is OCCUPIED: Mavi et al. 2511.07364 (stepwise confidence for failure detection, AUC-ROC ~0.9, LIVE-VERIFIED) and Vasudev et al. 2602.03338 (LLM critic AUROC 0.94 on agent failure, LIVE-VERIFIED). At those calibration levels the packet's OWN sweep model predicts the monitor LOSES (flip-point requires confidence AUROC < 0.72; published stepwise evaluators sit at ~0.9).
- The claim's load-bearing distinguisher — measured LEAD TIME beating self-confidence — is FALSIFIED by the project's own evidence: EXP-0033 d(mon−conf) = −0.006 CI [−0.011,−0.001]; lead-time coverage 42% < pre-registered 0.5 bar.
- The one robust positive (+0.095 vs static difficulty) is the LEAST-novel half, implicit in any PRM step-scoring (Lightman 2305.20050) or progress-rate metric (AgentBoard, Ma NeurIPS'24) — it is the trivially-expected gap between a time-resolved online signal and a t=0 static predictor (theory_skeptic: information-set-asymmetry tautology).
